	"_note": "Demo fixture. DRESSED, 2026-08-10. Guardrails round the upper deck plate and three sides of its stairwell (the fourth is where stair 8 arrives); a mast with radome, whips, floodlights and three stays on the deckhouse roof; a banded exhaust stack; a knuckle-boom crane whose two-part boom is ONE spar polyline, with hoist and hook block; a pair of curved davits with falls and blocks; sidelights on the deckhouse corners; three fenders on lanyards over the starboard side; four mooring bitts. 74 items, all spar and wire. COST: draw calls UNCHANGED at 8, triangles 9083 -> 11443 (+26%). ROOM PURGE 2026-08-10: the room primitive was deleted and this fixture's deckhouse went with it. What remains is the bare hull rig — bulwark walls, deck plates, stairs and items. Fittings that stood on the deckhouse now stand in open air on purpose; the superstructure is rebuilt from the sloped-plate primitive in the next wave, not re-authored out of walls. The three mast stays (ids 244-246) were belayed to the deckhouse roof and were deleted with it: a stay whose lower end is made fast to nothing is a line to nowhere, which tests/vessel_render_capture.gd rightly refuses. The mast keeps its whips, radome and floodlights.",
